    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n33294" root="فذ" body-key="f">
    
      4 
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">افذّهُ</span></b>  <i>He made him,</i> or <i>it, to be single; sole;</i>
or <i>one, and no more;</i> syn. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَوْتَرَهُ</span>; (S in art. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وتر</span>;)
and <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">جَعَلَهُ فَذًّا</span>, i. e. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">وِتْراً</span>. (TA in that art.) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2- 
And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">أَفَذَّتْ</span> <i>She</i> (a ewe or goat) <i>brought forth
one only,</i> (El-Ahmar, T, S, M, O, L, Msb,) <i>at a
breeding;</i> (Msb;) inf. n. <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">إِفْذَاذٌ</span>. (El-Ahmar, T,
M, L.) [See <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">مُفِذٌّ</span>.]

